# Chaos: a container window the server opened is never thrown away for lack of side panel room (O485, owner 2026-11-11;
# client/BASE.md "0191"; modules/game_interface/gameinterface.lua, modules/game_containers/containers.lua; after 0001-0190).
# Lua only, no engine code. The red line "There is no available space." that a player read as bag space was the client's own:
# addToPanels closed the new window and blamed "space" when no side panel had room for one more mini window.
#  * addToPanels(widget, room): with room == 'always' a window no panel has room for is placed by the pure
#    ChaosPanelRoom.plan (overlay game_chaoslayout, panelroom_logic.lua, tested by panelroom_test.lua): other open
#    container windows shrink towards their minimum height (the biggest first), then other resizable mini windows, in the panel
#    with the most room, only as far as the room needed; if even that is not enough the window goes in anyway (the panel with
#    the most room, everything shrinkable at its minimum, as a priority window is forced). Nothing is closed.
#  * containers.lua: both addToPanels calls of onContainerOpen pass 'always'. A refusal of the container is no longer possible.
#  * fitPanelWithoutClosing(panel): the same shrink for a panel whose windows overflow it (called by game_chaoslayout after a
#    login restore); no-op when they fit.
#  * the text of the failure line (every other window that does not fit): "No room in the side panels. Close or shrink a
#    window." (pt-BR in client_chaos_locale); it said "space", which sounded like the bag.
# Without game_chaoslayout (no ChaosPanelRoom) a container window is forced on the first panel. Not run in a client.
